lowers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-18T17:08:10Z","updated_at":"2026-09-18T17:08:10Z","body":"> Afaik changing argument names breaks compatibility with C#\r\n\r\nWould be a source-breaking change (for those who used named parameters) but not a binary-breaking change. So C# libraries/packages targeting previous Godot versions would remain compatible, but if existing C# code was re-compiled for newer Godot versions, it would error if named parameters `pos`, `size` or `dcColor` were used.\r\n\r\nNamed parameters are usually used to avoid having to pass default parameters. In this case, naming some of these parameters would skip several default parameters (e.g. naming `size` in `DrawStringOutline` would skip `alignment`, `width` and `fontSize`).\r\n\r\nI'm not sure if it's worth it to rename them now, but I agree with the new names.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5733454773/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]